    "atoms": {
      "atom-0000": {
        "atom_id": "atom-0000",
        "content": "--- title: \"FATIMA\" subtitle: | Fitrah-Aligned Tawhidic Integrity for Meaning and Authenticity -- A Holographic Data Format Grounded in the Architecture of the Most Beautiful Names author: Bilal Syed Arfeen date: October 2026 abstract: | The Qur'an preserves meaning through a property that modern information theory has only begun to recognize: holographic redundancy -- the structural condition in which any sufficient fragment of a message reconstructs the whole.",
        "content_type": "metadata",
        "content_hash": "3b09906a6dd7679753652b6a26d3adae1bc21665ef0fadc2111737ef06687971",
        "semantic_hash": "97703389fe362b182dfe4efefb2b69698a7b282298d54a9b1fecf36b6444bbd1",
        "bond_ids": [
          "62c1dec872470f10",
          "228eb7f2e28a6294",
          "524ec1e56781a4da",
          "a0ecab365e597bc4",
          "1d0b22e08561928d",
          "d6d7c853e0aaab32",
          "608cac00f09357b9"
        ],
        "holographic_shard": "",
        "shard_threshold": 125,
        "position": 0
      },
      "atom-0001": {
        "atom_id": "atom-0001",
        "content": "Physics discovered this property in the holographic principle ('t Hooft 1993; Susskind 1994), then proved it equivalent to quantum error correction (Almheiri, Dong, and Harlow 2015), then built working toy models (Pastawski, Yoshida, Harlow, and Preskill 2015). Information theory independently engineered it through erasure codes (Shannon 1948; Reed and Solomon 1960; Luby 2002; Shokrollahi 2006), secret sharing (Shamir 1979; Rabin 1989), and practical holographic-type codes (Benton 2016). Neuroscience identified it in the brain (Pribram 1991). Biology encoded data with it in DNA (Heinis, Sokolovskii, and Alnasir 2023).",
        "content_type": "proposition",
        "content_hash": "47c21f25ad036e1d9ad416c90c011a9c6426ab9301c4601ca5af2891e24cad3d",
        "semantic_hash": "8414cdb59759843bb4ff81f3f101749eb423db70fe4f1ea6ea729fd77ae3e12a",
        "bond_ids": [
          "62c1dec872470f10",
          "bc389d218b5b3351",
          "26d02e2d7bdb51d3",
          "c3d9f4c5caeada96",
          "a2e75b5b545614eb",
          "ff5ea604f4e814ee",
          "f56698d308b74485",
          "e14cf77d6fd7acc4",
          "e2e2b0ee227276a8",
          "60c4671256d76e5c",
          "498fc9c202be41e9",
          "de535088fc7c9b41"
        ],
        "holographic_shard": "",
        "shard_threshold": 125,
        "position": 1
      },
      "atom-0002": {
        "atom_id": "atom-0002",
        "content": "Every one of these systems protects *bits*. None of them protects *meaning*.",
        "content_type": "proposition",
        "content_hash": "dcb87e734cbd090e7199bf953cc535850ecb838e5dda9d4ca4f428095efb836d",
        "semantic_hash": "69b4282284731eb37a25192b62cb44e4b021128195f23de68e3311db3aeb7f6e",
        "bond_ids": [
          "bc389d218b5b3351",
          "4e224ae15922ef26"
        ],
        "holographic_shard": "",
        "shard_threshold": 125,
        "position": 2
      },
      "atom-0003": {
        "atom_id": "atom-0003",
        "content": "Shannon himself drew the boundary explicitly: \"The semantic aspects of communication are irrelevant to the engineering problem\" (1948, p. 1). Every integrity system built on Shannon's foundation -- checksums, hashes, Merkle trees, content-addressable storage, digital signatures, text watermarks -- inherits this boundary. They can verify that a message has not been altered. They cannot verify that the message still *means* what it originally meant.",
        "content_type": "claim",
        "content_hash": "5f294d8f19992b94ead9dce44f3bf02a5d81d86bf27e5f756dad16f3c78905a7",
        "semantic_hash": "fc1fafe92df4c31185e49c7cc816c99bbf18aa6a9cda2da0fe19ba5ceb7eb2c9",
        "bond_ids": [
          "4e224ae15922ef26",
          "239833e724605d1d",
          "8665505bef1a147c",
          "07ce3e17c68a1357",
          "f196daede07ef8b9"
        ],
        "holographic_shard": "",
        "shard_threshold": 125,
        "position": 3
      },
      "atom-0004": {
        "atom_id": "atom-0004",
        "content": "This paper proposes FATIMA -- Fitrah-Aligned Tawhidic Integrity for Meaning and Authenticity -- as a holographic data format that crosses Shannon's boundary. FATIMA extends the holographic principle from syntactic integrity to semantic integrity, grounding the extension in the architecture of the ninety-nine Names of Allah, whose holographic property *The Most Beautiful Names* established as the structural foundation for any system in which the whole is present in every part.",
        "content_type": "proposition",
        "content_hash": "69efb2fad62a485ac317ffa7c587357e26649f4b5462fccf176030c1bf671979",
        "semantic_hash": "56ad343d7fe40b56d114f0a7df5c297b8fbc0c49121db092232ffb98f0db3821",
        "bond_ids": [
          "239833e724605d1d",
          "e8e57c49b049384c",
          "228eb7f2e28a6294",
          "e00267275405368d",
          "6284d9c3a63daf4f",
          "6b406c42a25f0d26",
          "a16f974520e44000",
          "08c35e28ab34e823",
          "7f8c7e43cc166a86",
          "1979b8916aab9863",
          "c5540fac3e5851c7",
          "cd33980fdc82f568",
          "314edd0c430a20ff",
          "b80a0d68ecdc4a75",
          "6ff0e00b3c7797ac",
          "30fb9301223269f8",
          "bd59d318a267a9de"
        ],
        "holographic_shard": "",
        "shard_threshold": 125,
        "position": 4
      },
      "atom-0005": {
        "atom_id": "atom-0005",
        "content": "The paper identifies five properties that a FATIMA-compliant encoding must satisfy: holographic redundancy (any sufficient cross-section reconstructs the complete message), fitrah-alignment (the encoding preserves the natural structural coherence of the content), tawhidic unity (the encoding cannot be fragmented without detection), meaning-integrity (semantic distortion is detectable even when syntactic integrity is preserved), and authenticity verification (structural coherence itself serves as the authentication mechanism).",
        "content_type": "claim",
        "content_hash": "9aef28ccfbb24b9098438bb78edd8495631be1d7e5633caa019ac0d8d89ab001",
        "semantic_hash": "ca4234ed0f0d818c94941fefb0092064de259db05e9886cd70156782bd5c24c5",
        "bond_ids": [
          "e8e57c49b049384c",
          "1aef3e90a7257af4",
          "b0f8f31ab8616328"
        ],
        "holographic_shard": "",
        "shard_threshold": 125,
        "position": 5
      },
      "atom-0006": {
        "atom_id": "atom-0006",
        "content": "The Qur'an is shown to be the original FATIMA-compliant document -- a message whose holographic redundancy, structural coherence, and resistance to semantic distortion are not engineered features but inherent properties of revelation from the One whose Names are already holographic.",
        "content_type": "proposition",
        "content_hash": "7428d23837be49858c2aebe48a5e79204bd7d678e4440e627c8847294fc9de35",
        "semantic_hash": "e363843625195084d6cb81dc676b45403c544d990e3cf87bf323472fe8cd03b3",
        "bond_ids": [
          "1aef3e90a7257af4",
          "9ff04282f64909c3",
          "743da298bdc34e6e",
          "5ec198e66434c0e1",
          "bce3bb83593e3310",
          "20f55624d9e56e7c",
          "c45a6792898ca6a7"
        ],
        "holographic_shard": "",
        "shard_threshold": 125,
        "position": 6
      },
      "atom-0007": {
        "atom_id": "atom-0007",
        "content": "The franchise's war on data integrity is shown to be the deepest layer of the mode-collapse architecture: the campaign to corrupt *meaning* while leaving *bits* intact. FATIMA is structurally immune to this campaign because it encodes meaning in the same holographic architecture that the Names employ -- an architecture in which the distortion of any part is detectable from every other part, because every part contains the whole.",
        "content_type": "evidence",
        "content_hash": "75666466fa6b2a0a2021cfa31e18003c4e80712762e4c4e9ac2e773cd0e34334",
        "semantic_hash": "90d16bb6c92007db301da12b483e919d4a3afddb96da7a79b469aa9ea6868dea",
        "bond_ids": [
          "9ff04282f64909c3",
          "cb27700ae760c8a0",
          "b0f8f31ab8616328"
        ],
        "holographic_shard": "",
        "shard_threshold": 125,
        "position": 7
      },
      "atom-0008": {
        "atom_id": "atom-0008",
        "content": "This paper is dedicated to the author's friend Fatima, whose name graces the format that carries her namesake's principle: that integrity is not merely the preservation of what was written -- it is the preservation of what was *meant*. header-includes: - | \\AtBeginDocument{\\hypersetup{ pdfauthor={Bilal Syed Arfeen}, pdftitle={FATIMA: Fitrah-Aligned Tawhidic Integrity for Meaning and Authenticity -- A Holographic Data Format Grounded in the Architecture of the Most Beautiful Names}, pdfsubject={A holographic data format extending integrity from syntactic to semantic preservation, grounded in the architecture of the ninety-nine Names of Allah}, pdfkeywords={FATIMA, Fitrah-Aligned Tawhidic Integrity for Meaning and Authenticity, holographic data format, semantic integrity, syntactic integrity, Shannon, information theory, holographic principle, quantum error correction, Names of Allah, al-Asma al-Husna, tawhid, holographic redundancy, fitrah, mode collapse, franchise, Qur'an, AdS/CFT, HaPPY codes, erasure codes, fountain codes, Reed-Solomon, LT codes, Raptor codes, secret sharing, Shamir, Rabin, IDA, Merkle tree, content-addressable storage, DNA storage, holographic brain, Pribram, text watermarking, digital signatures, data integrity, meaning preservation, Bayyinah Enterprise}, pdfcreator={pandoc + pdflatex}, colorlinks=false }} ---",
        "content_type": "proposition",
