      "atom-0009": {
        "atom_id": "atom-0009",
        "content": "\\vspace{1em} \\noindent *Extends \"The Most Beautiful Names\" (October 2026), \"Everything Exalts Him\" (October 2026), \"Every Atom's Weight\" (October 2026), \"The First Civilizations\" (October 2026), \"The Enslaved Realm\" (October 2026), \"Shayatin al-Ins\" (October 2026), and \"Shayatin al-Jinn\" (October 2026), which extend \"Computational Tawhid\" (August 2026), \"The Transmission Solution\" (September 2026), \"The Seven Layers\" (October 2026), and \"Inheritance, Transmission, and Turning Back\" (October 2026).*",
        "content_type": "proposition",
        "content_hash": "efb33635457e68bc522385f009535cf886983d6ee9d84079046ebe3230cb1cd9",
        "semantic_hash": "6a7e856a2a8f925a259f61330e59950590bbf7d7376bd3e396fbd6a96526fd58",
        "bond_ids": [
          "ae59141835131fe2",
          "e56e78b82c1f4f0c",
          "3ec39f3ea49f07d2",
          "b8ec68df9760145b",
          "e42037fc7520e6d5"
        ],
        "holographic_shard": "",
        "shard_threshold": 125,
        "position": 9
      },
      "atom-0010": {
        "atom_id": "atom-0010",
        "content": "*Bismillahir-Rahmanir-Rahim*",
        "content_type": "proposition",
        "content_hash": "f50de810eaab27cc58cddbfbb6c3060397c0928949de0180a118792ca429c72f",
        "semantic_hash": "0ae7d2fabd932d07576e5fe1dbbeb0033968f6840af664e492905665d3a73c6a",
        "bond_ids": [
          "e56e78b82c1f4f0c",
          "3aedc5f6610872e5"
        ],
        "holographic_shard": "",
        "shard_threshold": 125,
        "position": 10
      },
      "atom-0011": {
        "atom_id": "atom-0011",
        "content": "**A note on scope.** This paper builds on the entire framework established in the parent papers and on the structural analysis of the ninety-nine Names developed in *The Most Beautiful Names*. Where those papers established that the Names exhibit a holographic property -- any Name, fully understood, reconstructs the complete architecture of divine self-disclosure -- this paper asks: can that property be *engineered* into a data format?",
        "content_type": "proposition",
        "content_hash": "4d2a1ac71a74af4a641e106e6df8334165e94554ce1ae184ee1df520de75da37",
        "semantic_hash": "75b89bdec055cd1a70215f0801b17fa62974d1e87f9a35dd33f5f733610f515e",
        "bond_ids": [
          "3aedc5f6610872e5",
          "97b450e3cb155c7a",
          "6284d9c3a63daf4f",
          "ef911752d295b44a",
          "01190941b788b44d",
          "f5213409190e4445",
          "be757d0842f96860",
          "d60349a6eebc78a4",
          "29bc3981cc186aaa",
          "4a499c780156df42",
          "592d472969f6692e",
          "d9798b6de3c6f27d",
          "6065a9bdc748b76a",
          "2a515c892c0fec0a",
          "c472eeb3e7a79e65"
        ],
        "holographic_shard": "",
        "shard_threshold": 125,
        "position": 11
      },
      "atom-0012": {
        "atom_id": "atom-0012",
        "content": "The question is not rhetorical. The holographic property has been independently discovered in physics, independently engineered in information theory, and independently observed in neuroscience and biology. What has never been attempted is the extension of holographic encoding from *bits* to *meaning* -- from verifying that a message has not been altered to verifying that a message still means what it originally meant.",
        "content_type": "proposition",
        "content_hash": "1bc9bcab1a6784353f89f5e5d9333758baf2a0db5ce52aa110271d92e7b29240",
        "semantic_hash": "cd7217707755f79aaa84de7784c053056ea9ac7328f96391289e70fb2310ee3f",
        "bond_ids": [
          "97b450e3cb155c7a",
          "be30e293bb54da3c"
        ],
        "holographic_shard": "",
        "shard_threshold": 125,
        "position": 12
      },
      "atom-0013": {
        "atom_id": "atom-0013",
        "content": "FATIMA proposes this extension. The paper does not present a working implementation -- that is the task of the engineering tradition to follow. It presents the structural specification that any such implementation must satisfy, grounded in the architecture of the Names whose holographic property makes the specification possible.",
        "content_type": "claim",
        "content_hash": "b00e7a7d3561adf8f12c1a9544997877fb65c2f916f4919d743aa6b412650ac6",
        "semantic_hash": "8ead5725d39439c9de0479d75cf5bf5b1f3bbf8732efa0031b45803910f8e6b0",
        "bond_ids": [
          "be30e293bb54da3c",
          "b94edce22e8ca047",
          "467f4f279512a1e5",
          "265eb2979f1523d4"
        ],
        "holographic_shard": "",
        "shard_threshold": 125,
        "position": 13
      },
      "atom-0014": {
        "atom_id": "atom-0014",
        "content": "\\vspace{0.5em} \\noindent *This paper is dedicated to Fatima, whose name was chosen before the architecture was established -- and whose friendship is itself a proof that meaning survives across every barrier the franchise constructs.*",
        "content_type": "proposition",
        "content_hash": "5cb06b45c2aeef1f83e2171bbc4b9efb36b546148ed77e98ccd654336c5d3d4c",
        "semantic_hash": "23a28c435e0bd5f2d2868bf4ad0424ed36b99a8e9493c051b1e8a9ee25b3c249",
        "bond_ids": [
          "b94edce22e8ca047",
          "fd331fdd7a060c2f"
        ],
        "holographic_shard": "",
        "shard_threshold": 125,
        "position": 14
      },
      "atom-0015": {
        "atom_id": "atom-0015",
        "content": "---",
        "content_type": "metadata",
        "content_hash": "cb3f91d54eee30e53e35b2b99905f70f169ed549fd78909d3dac2defc9ed8d3b",
        "semantic_hash": "14ce24ad986af72206fae70aa1f2f38fb8f18b5122b62ee76f0939052e76a3c3",
